Matthew Lahut's praying spoiler
(http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html) implies that this is
true:

--
"An object appears at your feet!" - you could have prayed (barring bad
luck, as usual) but now can't, because receiving an artifact adds to
your prayer timeout.
--

So you will only receive an artifact when your prayer timeout is zero.
If you keep praying whenever you can, your chances of getting an
artifact are not very good because all your sacrifices will go towards
decreasing your prayer timeout. So it's not a good idea to pray at all
during a sac-fest if you can help it. Since you only have two
artifacts (if you've done the quest, three), you should be able to get
at least one or two more from saccing, possibly even more if you're
patient. If you're lucky, you'll get Frostbrand or Mjollnir or some
other, more worthy weapon.

